+\section{Outlook}
+
+The fixed-parameter construction above gives sectorial solutions at infinity
+with controlled remainders, while the strong-drive analysis identifies the
+local Weber comparison and the first two fixed-level energy scales.  What
+remains is a univalent finite chain of Weber, Airy, and endpoint domains.  It
+would control the error variation on a global matching domain and permit
+evaluation of the associated origin connection data.  The
+exact entireness condition in Section~\ref{sec:heunwi} is the rigorous scalar
+spectral condition during that analysis.  Generic DCHE series, limiting procedures, and connection
+techniques provide useful comparison points
+\cite{Buhring1994DCHE,ElJaickFigueiredo2008Solutions,
+ElJaickFigueiredo2013Coulomb,IshkhanyanEtAl2014DCHE,Leaver1986Spectral}, but
+their convergence domains and parameter assumptions must first be rechecked for
+the present \(\varepsilon_{\rm D}=0\), ramified case.  The derived
+characteristic condition permits controlled
+evaluation of \(\Psi(z)\), its zeros, and its logarithmic magnitude on expanding
+compact subsets of the complex plane without direct matrix diagonalization.
+The resulting holomorphic functions and their zero and modulus geometry should
+then be compared explicitly with earlier coherent-state plots, Husimi and
+Wigner representations, semiclassical quasienergy contours, and Floquet
+descriptions \cite{MaslovaEtAl2019Squeezing,KirchmairEtAl2013Kerr}.
+
+The sectorial asymptotic solutions developed above and the exact
+spectral condition of Section~\ref{sec:heunwi} require no knowledge of the global
+connection.  The latter remains an open question, which the exploratory
+WKB analysis suggests but does not prove.  Resolution of the connection
+problem is deferred to future work.
+
